Administrative divisions","content":"8 districts; Creek, Eastern, Midland, South Town, Spot Bay, Stake Bay, West End, Western","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:42","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:43","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Constitution Day, first Monday in July","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:44","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"1959; revised 1962, 1972, and 1994","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:45","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"British common law and local statutes","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:46","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"18 years of age; universal","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:47","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: Queen ELIZABETH II (since 6 February 1952); Governor Stuart JACK (since 23 November 2005)\n\nhead of government: Leader of Government Business Kurt TIBBETTS (since 18 May 2005)\n\ncabinet: Executive Council (three members appointed by the governor, four members elected by the Legislative Assembly)\n\nelections: none; the monarch is hereditary; the governor is appointed by the monarch; following legislative elections, the leader of the majority party or coalition is appointed by the governor Leader of Government Business","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:48","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral Legislative Assembly (18 seats, 3 appointed members from the Executive Council and 15 elected by popular vote; members serve four-year terms)\n\nelections: last held 11 May 2005 (next to be held in 2009)\n\nelection results: percent of vote by party - NA; seats by party - PPM 9, UDP 5, independent 1","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:49","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Summary Court; Grand Court; Cayman Islands Court of Appeal","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:50","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"no national teams (loose groupings of political organizations) were formed for the 2000 elections; United Democratic Party or UDP [leader McKeeva BUSH]; People's Progressive Movement or PPM [leader Kurt TIBBETTS]","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:51","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"NA","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:52","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"Caricom (associate), CDB, Interpol (subbureau), IOC, UNESCO (associate), UPU","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:53","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:54","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:55","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"blue, with the flag of the UK in the upper hoist-side quadrant and the Caymanian coat of arms centered on the outer half of the flag; the coat of arms includes a pineapple and turtle above a shield with three stars (representing the three islands) and a scroll at the bottom bearing the motto HE HATH FOUNDED IT UPON THE SEAS","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:56","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"With no direct taxation, the islands are a thriving offshore financial center. More than 40,000 companies were registered in the Cayman Islands as of 1998, including almost 600 banks and trust companies; banking assets exceed $500 billion. A stock exchange was opened in 1997. Tourism is also a mainstay, accounting for about 70% of GDP and 75% of foreign currency earnings. The tourist industry is aimed at the luxury market and caters mainly to visitors from North America. Total tourist arrivals exceeded 1.2 million in 1997, with 600,000 from the US. About 90% of the islands' food and consumer goods must be imported. The Caymanians enjoy one of the highest outputs per capita and one of the highest standards of living in the world.","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:57","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$1.939 billion (2004 est.)","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:58","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (official exchange rate)","content":"NA","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:59","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"0.9% (2004 est.)","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:60","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita (PPP)","content":"$43,800 (2004 est.)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2006/geos/cj.html#field:61","country":"KY","edition_year":2006},{"category":"economy","label"